course: dictionary
lesson: 11823
title: Birdsong and mood
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Birdsong is the musical sound birds make, most of all in the early morning and in spring. You can often work out a word like this from the words around it. «The garden was full of birdsong when we opened the window.» Full of and opened the window tell you it is a sound you can hear, and it comes from birds.
explain: Look for clues about time. «At dawn, the birdsong began before the sun had risen.» Dawn is the start of the day, so birdsong here means the early morning songs. In stories and poems, birdsong often creates a calm, peaceful mood, or tells the reader that it is morning.
explain: In science, birdsong helps people identify birds, because each kind sings in its own way. Birds also sing to mark their territory, the area they claim as their own, and to attract a mate. The phrase «the dawn chorus» means lots of birdsong at sunrise.
fact: Birdsong is a noun, and it is uncountable: you say some birdsong, not a birdsong.
fact: «Birdsong» means the musical sounds birds make, especially in the early morning and in spring.
fact: «The dawn chorus» means lots of birdsong at sunrise.
fact: In science, birdsong can help identify birds and show how they mark their territory and attract a mate.
fact: In poems and stories, birdsong can create a calm, peaceful mood or show that it is morning.
exercise: «The garden was full of birdsong on spring mornings.» What is birdsong? | The rain on the window | The sound of a car engine | The buzzing of bees in the flowers | *The musical sounds that birds make
exercise: «The dawn chorus filled the woods before sunrise.» What does the phrase dawn chorus mean? | *Lots of birdsong at sunrise | A loud thunderstorm at night | A choir singing in church | Birds flying south for winter
exercise: «Birdsong made the morning feel calm and peaceful.» What mood does the birdsong create here? | Busy and rushed | *Calm and peaceful | Angry and noisy | Scary and dark
test: Scientists listened to the birdsong in the forest to find out which birds lived there. Why is birdsong useful in science? | To make the birds fly away | To measure the rain | To paint the trees | *To help identify birds
test: Birds sing in spring. According to the lesson, why do they sing? | To escape from cats | To warm up the sun | *To attract a mate and mark their territory | To count the trees
exam: Which word means the musical sounds birds make? | Birdbath | Birdseed | Birdcage | *Birdsong
